PasClaw vendors the following MIT-licensed source files in
src/pkg/vendor/zpaq/:

  libzpaq.pas
  ZpaqClasses.pas
  ZpaqSimple.pas
      Free Pascal port of LIBZPAQ Version 7.15 (Aug. 17, 2016)
      Port by Xelitan (www.xelitan.com)
      https://github.com/Xelitan/Free-Pascal-port-of-LIBZPAQ-Version-7.15

The port bundles code from three upstream projects under MIT and public
domain licenses (all listed in libzpaq.pas + LICENSE):

  libdivsufsort (C) 2003-2008 Yuta Mori        -- MIT
  libtomcrypt   (C) 2001-2017 Tom St. Denis    -- public domain
  Salsa20/8         D. Bernstein               -- public domain
  LibZPaq           Matt Mahoney                -- public domain
      http://mattmahoney.net/zpaq/

The Pascal port itself is distributed under the MIT License (see
LICENSE in this directory).

These units back PasClaw.Checkpoints.Zpaq (src/pkg/checkpoints/) --
the snapshot store that powers /undo + /redo. The port is written in
{$mode objfpc} so it compiles only under Free Pascal; Delphi builds
fall back to the legacy blob-tree checkpoint backend documented in
docs/checkpoints.md.

No modifications were made to the upstream sources beyond placing them
in this directory. The demo program (zpaq.lpr) and Lazarus project
file (zpaq.lpi) are NOT vendored since we drive the library through
its Pascal API rather than the CLI. Updates can be re-vendored
verbatim from upstream.
